{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\n\\mathcal{O} \\otimes_{p, f_pf_*\\mathcal{O}} f_p\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PMod}(f_*\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$c_\\mathcal{O} : f_pf_*\\mathcal{O} \\to \\mathcal{O}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-presheaf-module}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-presheaf-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoint-pull-push-presheaves-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6c7a8f4fa8a7a68390a31c2000c954a5d67b823904ddf94d576456900791b784", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:68e09506e39c983b868dfecaac1008fb2864b566b5a1b41d6cbe2f60dbdaf62e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a presheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a presheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a presheaf of <MATH_0007>-modules.\nThen\n<MATH_0008>\nHere we use\nLemmas <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>, and we use\nthe map <MATH_0009>\nin the definition of the tensor product.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:373815b2384cc23f8691d0764fc615442fff9443735bfc0a6493314fbc001ba2", "unit_id": "tag:008V:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\n\\mathcal{O} \\otimes_{p, f_pf_*\\mathcal{O}} f_p\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PMod}(f_pf_*\\mathcal{O})}(\nf_p\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}_{f_pf_*\\mathcal{O}}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PMod}(f_*\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{G},\nf_*(\\mathcal{F}_{f_pf_*\\mathcal{O}})) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PMod}(f_*\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "MATH_0002": "$f_*(\\mathcal{F}_{f_pf_*\\mathcal{O}}) = f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{id}_{f_*\\mathcal{O}}$", "MATH_0005": "$c_\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{id}_{f_*\\mathcal{O}} = f_*c_\\mathcal{O} \\circ i_{f_*\\mathcal{O}}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-adjointness-tensor-restrict-presheaves}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint-push-pull-presheaves-modules}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-presheaves}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4dba6f652c85dbbb44d60aa67d5aab0c3180e59b481352769084948cc14981af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2b08814cdfddc3aceae78234e68f206c8d74ca791421920e309c2249222bf4d2", "source_text": "This follows from the equalities\n<MATH_0001>\nThe first equality is\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThe second equality is\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThe third equality is given by the equality\n<MATH_0002>\nof abelian sheaves which is <MATH_0003>-linear. Namely,\n<MATH_0004> corresponds to <MATH_0005>\nunder the adjunction described in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0003>\nand thus\n<MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d36c8f677fb43b229914b4851521ffde00731665d2ee43e9080954f53758c34", "unit_id": "tag:008V:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-presheaf-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pushforward-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:521646d7704c3a199a4306cb166106629da554f6c67f76fc9429c7ee4e1edb6f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f30c519800b376f1b318c22b029680d5d325f762d175296d9d88325b9a337699", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>. Let\n<MATH_0004> be a sheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nThe pushforward <MATH_0006>, as defined in\nLemma <REF_0001>\nis a sheaf of <MATH_0007>-modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:589e510dc43c659aeb88c5822353675d409099b788d9e557a2c44df119a9c01f", "unit_id": "tag:008W:statement"}
