{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{O} \\times f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}\n\\longrightarrow\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{G}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0008": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:32751c5abf11aee862f03a92735a443785fa9726c1730f367d42c03cb8be6244", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0e28f8a92c2f9a890165ea4ed752349d6b86812be5921ee8f8653fb6e37cdb65", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>. Let\n<MATH_0004> be a sheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nThere is a natural map of underlying presheaves of sets\n<MATH_0006>\nwhich turns <MATH_0007> into a\nsheaf of <MATH_0008>-modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b8f19fa68eaa7bc498f2ba2a2c9b51087b7b6b69864602f21aff4b21d2466f4", "unit_id": "tag:008X:statement"}
